1
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,219
Come on in.

2
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:16,307
A WHILE AGO

3
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:21,479
I'll move your doctor's appointment.

4
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,148
Mmm.

5
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,989
It's been a while, Mr. Minamoto.

6
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:36,953
Yes, it has.

7
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,042
Do you remember him?

8
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,966
Your son is all grown up.

9
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:55,513
What I've heard, he's...

10
00:00:56,973 --> 00:01:00,185
he's been crafting
some pretty elaborate murders.

11
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:10,487
And why are you telling me this?

12
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:15,033
I want to know if you will kill him.

13
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,871
Before he goes too far.

14
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:23,625
You can make it look like an accident.

15
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,418
Or get a cop to do it.
I don't see any issue with that--

16
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:27,796
Forgive me for asking...

17
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:30,882
but why would I?

18
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:34,677
I'll see myself out.

19
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:38,848
He administers Speed K to his victims.

20
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:43,310
Then he kills them
by twisting their limbs around.

21
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:44,771
At least, that's what I've heard.

22
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:48,024
Oh, that reminds me.

23
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:52,612
Speed K's the very drug you developed,
wasn't it?

24
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:00,077
I just find it hard to believe

25
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:05,416
someone like you would be okay with our
shared history being aired out like that?

26
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:10,088
After all, that very history
is the reason you and I are even here.

27
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,603
Then, if I kill your son for you...

28
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,401
I'd like your help
with my business in return.

29
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:28,750
THE BLUE ROAD

30
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:36,299
<i>Seok.</i>

31
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,471
What is it?

32
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:45,016
Do you still hear the bells,
even after the ritual?

33
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:48,144
Well, are you afraid?

34
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,980
That you'll never stop hearing them?

35
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:57,779
<i>Yes.</i>

36
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:00,698
I'm scared, Uncle.

37
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,787
What if I hear...

38
00:04:07,121 --> 00:04:08,915
those bells everywhere I go?

39
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:13,253
You're only scared
because you choose to see them as scary.

40
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:17,006
But, Seok...

41
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:22,637
try to think of them as more like a...
like a form of companion?

42
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:26,099
They won't be so scary then.

43
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,227
No, in fact, they'll be your friends.

44
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:31,020
They'll help you.

45
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:35,149
Just like I will.

46
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,571
So do not fear.

47
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,160
Do not fear.

48
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:50,915
Do not fear.

49
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,087
Is he talking to himself?

50
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:59,173
- He seems nuts.
- Let's sit somewhere else.

51
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:44,052
Snap out of it.

52
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:50,933
Snap out of it.

53
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:01,527
Seo Hyun-tae.

54
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:03,988
Minamoto.

55
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,533
Minamoto Shunsuke. Hong Du-yeong.

56
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,383
INCHEON PORT, CHEONGHAE SHIPYARD,
MV MIRAE

57
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:24,884
Huh?

58
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:33,893
Cheonghae Shipyard...

59
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:35,645
Cheonghae Shipyard...

60
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:37,814
MV <i>Mirae</i>.

61
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,955
PROFESSOR JANG, THIS IS KIM SEOK

62
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,748
I'M WRITING TO ASK YOU A FAVOR.

63
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,209
THERE'S NO ONE ELSE
I CAN TRUST RIGHT NOW

64
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:10,179
<i>Hey, Kim Seok. Are you there?</i>

65
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:14,724
Kim Seok.

66
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:15,935
Are you in there?

67
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:21,983
Yes, gimme a minute, please.

68
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:41,042
Oh, for fuck's sake!

69
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,129
Kim Seok! Freeze!

70
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:46,048
Don't move.

71
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:02,689
That crazy son of a bitch.

72
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,150
The window! He went out the window!

73
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,741
<i>Ha In-beom! Did you get him?</i>

74
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,826
<i>Where are you?</i>

75
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:16,578
In-beom.

76
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,706
Seok, someone reported you
as a drug trafficker.

77
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:24,754
You're under arrest for drug possession
with intent to distribute.

78
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:29,841
- You really believe that?
- Come on, of course not!

79
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:30,927
I had no choice!

80
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:34,013
They ordered us to investigate you
no matter what.

81
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:38,017
You think I volunteered for this?

82
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:46,567
Jesus.

83
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:53,741
Let's go, kid.

84
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:57,370
What kind of cop

85
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,581
takes the side of a fugitive?

86
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,710
But you're not
actually the suspect, right?

87
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:08,464
Forget it.

88
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:21,601
Where is he?

89
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:22,686
Hey!

90
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,939
Kim Seok! Where'd he go? Damn it.

91
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:31,279
Did he get away or did you let him go?

92
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:34,949
Nicely done.

93
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,743
Shit.

94
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:44,166
I'm spending so much money on flights.

95
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,295
I'm sending you an invoice.

96
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:54,677
Inose. I know you're there. Open up.

97
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:02,310
Inose! I know you're in there!

98
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,398
What?

99
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:16,240
Whoa... how the hell
did you find out my passcode?

100
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:18,618
Forgive the intrusion.

101
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:23,539
Zero, five, two, nine.

102
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:25,875
That's your daughter's birthday, isn't it?

103
00:10:34,925 --> 00:10:37,762
And just when I switched over
to a digital lock...

104
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:41,057
so Rumi could come by whenever she wants.

105
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:46,062
Hey, why are you looking through my stuff?

106
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,985
So, where are you off to this time?

107
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:02,912
Well, gonna tell me what brought you here?

108
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:05,456
Korean National Intelligence Service?

109
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,210
So, Inspector Kim Seok.

110
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,507
Oh? Inspector Kim?

111
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:18,010
Well, seems like
he's now become a wanted criminal.

112
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:21,846
A what?

113
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:24,809
Apparently, it's for violating
the Narcotics Control Act.

114
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,437
And now he's fled
to avoid having to face the charges.

115
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:34,360
Speed K.

116
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:44,745
So, Ito Makoto, Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.

117
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:47,206
Korean and Japanese Intelligence.

118
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:52,294
The scale of this is insane, huh?

119
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:56,132
Who the hell
was this Minamoto Shunsuke anyway?

120
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,844
Goddamn it, Inose, take this seriously!

121
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:02,595
Korean National Intelligence Service
came here.

122
00:12:02,596 --> 00:12:05,558
That means the Japanese and Korean
superiors are monitoring this.

123
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,519
So, if you do anything reckless,

124
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:12,022
it might affect your ex-wife
and even Rumi.

125
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:14,650
How dare you? How dare you?

126
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,486
Inose.

127
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,739
I'm suspending you.

128
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:24,160
Tomorrow, you'll come to the station
to turn in your gun.

129
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,247
This is your final warning.

130
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:30,332
Don't even think about going to Korea!

131
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:34,503
In fact, stop doing anything for a while.

132
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:40,301
You need some time off.
Just go play pachinko or something.

133
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:52,021
CHEONGHAE SHIPYARD

134
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,593
MV <i>Mirae</i>?

135
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:36,774
Where the hell am I going?

136
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:49,202
Hello, old friend. Been a while.

137
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,704
Look, they're singing!

138
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,668
I should just be a pachinko player
instead of a detective.

139
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,710
<i>You got it!</i>

140
00:13:57,711 --> 00:13:58,962
BONUS TIME

141
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:00,297
<i>Super lucky!</i>

142
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:02,466
I won!

143
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:07,304
Whoa, check it out! Congratulations!

144
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,348
- I didn't cheat, I swear.
- Oh man, seriously?

145
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:12,350
None of you guys have even won anything.

146
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,270
Here, why don't you guys take this.

147
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,981
- No, don't want it.
- Here, take it, go on.

148
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,609
How are you? Sir, over here.

149
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:23,403
My apologies. Excuse me for a moment.

150
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:25,363
Could I perhaps
have a moment of your time?

151
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,949
Huh?

152
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:32,704
If you wouldn't mind following me
to our VIP suite with zero betting limit.

153
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:35,165
Oh, that sounds fantastic. Yeah?

154
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:39,253
All right.

155
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:43,882
Hey, you. Buddy, over here.
Save my spot for me.

156
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:45,009
Ooh.

157
00:14:51,181 --> 00:14:52,182
Come in, sir.

158
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:56,395
Oh...

159
00:14:57,396 --> 00:15:00,190
This sure looks like the VIP room,
all right.

160
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:05,279
With so many VIPs here, too...

161
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:21,128
Hmm.

162
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:23,087
Mm-mm-mmm.

163
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,173
Sir...

164
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:27,927
I don't know
what kind of bullshit you pulled.

165
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:31,387
But you better cough up
all your winnings and get out.

166
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:34,641
You are now officially
banned from the premises.

167
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:38,854
I don't see Ito or Li Yoon-ok.
And those walls seem pretty soundproof.

168
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:47,154
Listen, you. Who even are you?

169
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,532
I'll hand over my winnings, don't stress.

170
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:54,036
What?

171
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:58,540
But only if you tell me about Ito.

172
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:08,258
- You're a funny little guy, aren't you?
- Who does he think he is? Smug prick.

173
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,220
Eh, I gotta turn this in anyway...

174
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:15,724
- What the hell! Is that real?
- Hey! Whoa!

175
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,810
- I'm calling the police!
- The police?

176
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,395
I am the police, you little shit.

177
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:22,481
Want me to clean
this whole place out, huh?

178
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,151
Where's Ito?

179
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,864
We have no idea!

180
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:34,701
They never tell us where the boss is,
we swear it!

181
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:36,203
Oh...

182
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,999
I swear, we don't know!

183
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:46,046
Where is Ito?

184
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,549
- Where is he? Tell me!
- Hong Kong.

185
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,509
Hong Kong!

186
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,179
Hong Kong?

187
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:07,818
HONG KONG

188
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:37,305
SEO HYUN-TAE IS IN HK.
WILL GET BACK TO YOU SOON.

189
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,183
Who in the world is helping me?

190
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:58,327
<i>Hello?</i>

191
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:01,872
Prof-- Hello, Professor Jang. Kim Seok.

192
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:03,623
<i>Ah, Detective Kim.</i>

193
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:06,000
I was worried.
I haven't been able to reach you.

194
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,252
<i>Right. Sorry about that.</i>

195
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:09,962
So, uh, remember that email that I sent?

196
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:11,422
Of course. Your request.

197
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:13,092
Yes, I'm there now.

198
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:17,012
I brought up that name
you mentioned to your mother and...

199
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:18,889
Just a moment.

200
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:26,354
Once she heard it, she started screaming.

201
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:27,564
She had a seizure.

202
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:31,276
Her pulse skyrocketed. It was sheer chaos.

203
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,572
They gave her a sedative.
She's resting now.

204
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,492
But one thing is absolutely definite.

205
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:46,083
She knows him.

206
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,044
This Seo Hyun-tae person.

207
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:52,630
<i>Once she heard the name,
she started calling out,</i>

208
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:54,340
<i>"Du-yeong! Du-yeong!"</i>

209
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:56,218
<i>She then collapsed and started seizing.</i>

210
00:18:57,678 --> 00:19:00,097
Do you wanna know how Hong Du-yeong died?

211
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,810
Or would you rather know why?

212
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,650
All right. I see.

213
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:16,070
Thank you, Professor.
I'll return the favor, I promise.

214
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,531
<i>Oh, one more thing.</i>

215
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,410
<i>Remember those documents
we discussed last time?</i>

216
00:19:22,077 --> 00:19:24,245
<i>The Tiger Unit, the one called Tora.</i>

217
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:25,330
Yes.

218
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:29,667
I did some research on what else
had been written on the subject.

219
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:33,172
Certain elements of it
were kept in practice,

220
00:19:33,881 --> 00:19:35,674
even after the end of the occupation.

221
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:37,425
Mmm...

222
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:39,011
What do you mean, "elements"?

223
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:43,265
<i>Their torture methods, for example,
or how they'd drug their victims.</i>

224
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:47,226
It looks like those methods
were deliberately preserved

225
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:50,898
for the military or certain government
agencies to use during times of war.

226
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:54,984
In the 1980s,
the Agency for National Security Planning

227
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:58,864
operated under the guise of companies,
factories, print stores...

228
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:03,492
<i>But while undercover, they carried out
horrors that boggles the mind.</i>

229
00:20:03,493 --> 00:20:05,204
The ANSP were undercover?

230
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:07,247
A print store...

231
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:12,793
The ANSP arrested anyone involved
in the civic movement or student protests.

232
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:15,421
Mainly a number of college students,
social activists,

233
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:18,966
and even a few shamans who were
involved in anti-Japanese demonstrations.

234
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,971
The ANSP may have adopted
the Tiger Unit's methods of torture...

235
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,185
Anti-Japanese...

236
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:31,772
Shamans...

237
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:35,234
Anti-Japanese shamans...

238
00:20:57,297 --> 00:21:00,341
<i>Inose! What on earth are you up to now?</i>

239
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:02,677
<i>I told you to lay low, for God's sake!</i>

240
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,303
What are you talking about?

241
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,888
I'm doing what you asked.

242
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:08,349
I didn't go to Korea
and I accepted my suspension.

243
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,184
- <i>What I meant is--</i>
- Oh, please...

244
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:12,853
Who told me to go and play some pachinko
in the first place?

245
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:15,147
Hey! When did I ever tell you
to go cause trouble over there?

246
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:17,775
<i>Ah, well, those pricks
were trying to rip me off</i>

247
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:19,694
<i>so I figured
I'd just teach them</i> a <i>little lesson.</i>

248
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:20,778
You bastard.

249
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,781
I swear, Inose, you make my life just so...

250
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:24,700
I'm hanging up now.

251
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:30,038
Are you looking for Seo Hyun-tae?

252
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:33,458
Oh.

253
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:35,794
Hello, again.

254
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:38,297
Why are you...

255
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:45,052
You haven't been able to
reach Inspector Kim, have you?

256
00:21:45,053 --> 00:21:46,304
He's probably all over the place.

257
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,389
Kim Seok?

258
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:51,267
Uh... You know where he is?

259
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:54,771
No. Someone else is assigned to him, so...

260
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,068
What the hell?

261
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,363
Did you know that I was gonna be here?

262
00:22:04,781 --> 00:22:05,782
I had an inkling.

263
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:07,868
An inkling?

264
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:11,871
I figured you'd ignore my warning
and come anyway.

265
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:13,290
And you did, right?

266
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:17,419
So why don't you and I join forces?

267
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:24,760
Hey, wait. Hey!

268
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:27,387
Come on! We gotta catch Seo Hyun-tae!

269
00:22:35,062 --> 00:22:39,649
Did you know Hong Kong used to
be a tax haven for a lot of companies?

270
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:42,694
But... ...not anymore.

271
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:46,490
The vibe in Hong Kong has shifted a bit
since the handover from the UK.

272
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:54,789
Typical Japanese. You've zero interest
when it comes to foreign things.

273
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:55,956
Say what?

274
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:57,626
"Say what" is not very polite.

275
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:00,087
"Could you repeat that, please?"

276
00:23:03,298 --> 00:23:06,218
Well... I guess you've got
a lot on your mind right now.

277
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:08,929
I'm guessing you're wondering
if Kim Seok is here.

278
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:10,972
Whether or not he's okay...

279
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:14,809
Well, yeah.

280
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:17,269
I'm mainly just thinking if
Korean National Intelligence Service

281
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,189
really needed to stick your noses in this.

282
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:28,115
Speed K.

283
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,118
Huh?

284
00:23:32,494 --> 00:23:35,414
Seo Hyun-tae runs
the Northeast Asia drug cartel.

285
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:39,542
He's also been funneling
drugs into Korea too.

286
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:41,962
And we've been tracking him
for many years.

287
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:46,800
Both Korean and Japanese intelligence.

288
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:52,513
<i>He has the Speed K
manufactured in Central Asia,</i>

289
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:55,183
<i>and then routes it
through Hong Kong for distribution.</i>

290
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:58,854
<i>But as the government
cracked down on the cartel,</i>

291
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:03,900
<i>he found a work-around
by turning Speed K into a legal drug.</i>

292
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:07,028
<i>Like fentanyl.</i>

293
00:24:09,406 --> 00:24:10,406
Excuse me.

294
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:11,491
Yes?

295
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:15,035
I'm here to meet with your president
to confirm our deal.

296
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:16,871
- Oh, do you have an appointment?
- Yes.

297
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:18,123
Okay. Please wait.

298
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:25,129
<i>Today, Seo Hyun-tae will
sign a major contract</i>

299
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:26,840
<i>with Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.</i>

300
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:31,219
<i>But I don't know why Minamoto
decided to team up with Seo Hyun-tae.</i>

301
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:34,055
<i>They must have made some sort of deal.</i>

302
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:37,100
<i>The point is</i>

303
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:39,978
<i>we're catching Seo Hyun-tae tonight.</i>

304
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,493
<i>The thing is,</i>

305
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:58,872
I flew all this way
so I could apprehend a serial killer.

306
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:03,459
All this talk of drug investigations
and criminal organizations,

307
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,045
what do they have to do with this case?

308
00:25:09,382 --> 00:25:12,135
And who came up with
Emi Shunsuke's methods, huh?

309
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:20,893
Seo Hyun-tae was one of our senior agents.

310
00:25:20,894 --> 00:25:22,354
Come again?

311
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,357
Well, a sort of senior agent.

312
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:27,650
In the 80s,

313
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:31,821
he worked as an external contractor
for the Korean ANSP.

314
00:25:33,406 --> 00:25:34,950
The so-called print shop.

315
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:39,454
They kept it hidden because their methods
were too extreme even for the ANSP.

316
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:43,667
Some claim they got their torture methods
from the Japanese colonial era.

317
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:47,796
Where else would they have learned
to twist around their victims' limbs?

318
00:25:49,673 --> 00:25:51,299
And the first to think of it...

319
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:55,804
<i>might even have been...</i>

320
00:26:10,318 --> 00:26:11,319
The president says...

321
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:15,323
we're putting the contract on hold.

322
00:26:18,285 --> 00:26:20,829
Just until the results
from the clinical trial come in.

323
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:25,208
So, I suggest you leave now, quietly.

324
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:39,514
You're putting the contract on hold...

325
00:26:41,474 --> 00:26:42,934
until the trial results?

326
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:50,859
Hong Kong is nice, isn't it?

327
00:26:52,193 --> 00:26:53,236
Mr. Minamoto.

328
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:55,780
You pay less in taxes.

329
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,241
It's a good place to convalesce.

330
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:00,910
How dare you attack my men.

331
00:27:04,914 --> 00:27:06,541
Even a dirty mutt

332
00:27:07,584 --> 00:27:10,170
knows to watch its step around its master.

333
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:22,015
And yet you dare...

334
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:27,604
Well, a tiger can make
that same old mutt piss itself in fear.

335
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:34,944
You arrogant shit.
Who do you think you are?

336
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,156
You shut your mouth.

337
00:27:39,115 --> 00:27:40,617
It would be so easy.

338
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:44,829
I could rip
your pathetic little heart out right now.

339
00:27:47,123 --> 00:27:49,000
You wouldn't even fight back.

340
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:55,090
You damn Josenjing vermin.

341
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:04,140
After everything I've done,
you bite the hand that feeds you?

342
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:14,067
Persistent, isn't he?

343
00:28:17,278 --> 00:28:18,529
Hey.

344
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:20,407
You've been watching, right?

345
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:26,663
Don't kill him yet. Break his bones first.

346
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:29,916
Twist his limbs around.

347
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,168
Yes, sir. I will.

348
00:28:33,670 --> 00:28:34,796
This is morphine.

349
00:28:35,296 --> 00:28:37,132
To keep him alive until he talks.

350
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:40,927
- No... no, please...
- Damn Josenjing vermin.

351
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:44,347
Please, no more.

352
00:28:56,818 --> 00:28:58,445
To this day, you think that...

353
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,115
I haven't changed at all.

354
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,664
How many children do you have now?

355
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:12,875
After all,
you've fathered so many bastards,

356
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:16,337
you can't even remember which whore
gave birth to Shunsuke, can you?

357
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:21,634
His crimes would have sent
your company stock into a free fall.

358
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:25,096
And I...

359
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:29,350
I killed him for you.

360
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:32,854
That was our agreement.

361
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:36,232
You and I know the bulk of it wasn't you.

362
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,401
Those...

363
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:43,198
detectives did the heavy lifting,
you just finished him off.

364
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:48,787
Hey.

365
00:29:49,829 --> 00:29:50,830
Please, keep going.

366
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:56,085
The entire reason that boy
even became such a terrible monster...

367
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:58,880
was because of you, wasn't it?

368
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:18,441
More effective than opium, or poppies.

369
00:30:20,902 --> 00:30:23,863
What do you say? We do a clinical trial?

370
00:30:24,739 --> 00:30:25,865
Or...

371
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:29,202
you keep your promise after all.

372
00:30:30,119 --> 00:30:31,538
Goddamn bastard.

373
00:30:46,970 --> 00:30:48,972
K-HOTEL FRONT
REINA KASAHARA

374
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:54,518
Uh...

375
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:55,936
- Yes, sir?
- Excuse me.

376
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:57,021
Yes?

377
00:30:58,857 --> 00:30:59,858
Kasahara Reina.

378
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:01,526
My friend.

379
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:03,778
Would you mind waiting a moment?

380
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:18,418
You seem tired.

381
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:23,214
So, then was the contract
finalized in the end?

382
00:31:27,635 --> 00:31:28,636
Mmm.

383
00:31:30,638 --> 00:31:33,308
You've waited for this moment.
What an achievement.

384
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:36,852
I will get right to work,
just as soon as you give me the contract.

385
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:37,937
Yoon-ok.

386
00:31:41,357 --> 00:31:42,984
How exactly did Kim Seok...

387
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,405
manage to get away?

388
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:51,743
I'm sorry, sir.

389
00:31:53,244 --> 00:31:55,120
I thought for sure
our men would be able to--

390
00:31:55,121 --> 00:31:56,497
No, that's not what I mean.

391
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:01,501
The Korean police are on our tail.

392
00:32:01,502 --> 00:32:02,961
You have my word
that I'll tell my men to--

393
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:04,297
That's not what I mean, either.

394
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:12,388
You're not clumsy like that, not ever.

395
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:17,852
Right?

396
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:15,702
Sir, I...
